  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is subjected simultaneously to two SHMs, one along the <math><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and the other along the <math><mi>y</mi></math>-axis. The two vibrations are in phase and have unequal amplitudes. The particle will execute"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Straight line motion",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Circular motion",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Elliptic motion",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Parabolic motion",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the equations of the two mutually perpendicular SHM&#39;s of the same frequency and same phase be<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>&#160;sin&#160;</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Then,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>, which is the equation of a straight line</p>"
  }
